# Docker build-context exclusions (audit-3 R3-DEP-F1).
#
# The glm-ocr service builds with `context: .` (the repo ROOT) because its
# Dockerfile lives under docker/glm-ocr/. Without this file every build
# transmitted the ENTIRE working tree to the daemon — including `.env.local`
# and `.env.production.local`, which holds the hosted Supabase SERVICE-ROLE
# key. That is context transmission (the Dockerfile has no COPY), but it still
# ships secrets and multi-GB build output over the socket on every build,
# which is expensive on a remote/WSL2 `DOCKER_HOST` and a needless exposure on
# a shared build daemon. The sibling insightface service avoids the problem by
# using `context: ./docker/insightface`; this file gives glm-ocr the same
# protection without restructuring the build.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the repo's actual generated/secret paths.

# Secrets — never send to the daemon.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.example

# Dependencies / build output
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Test + coverage artifacts
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
snapshots
bench-glm-ocr.jsonl

# Local Supabase / tooling data
supabase/.temp
supabase/.branches
compreface-data

# VCS + agent scratch
.git
.gitignore
.github
.agents
.vscode
.idea
.tmp
.tmp_*

# Docs / design scratch (not needed by any Dockerfile today)
docs
design-system
redesign-previews
Sample Code
graphify-out
skills-lock.json
GEMINI.md
PROJECT.md
AGENTS.md

# Python bytecode (the insightface build context is its own dir, but keep the
# root context clean if a future Dockerfile builds from here).
__pycache__
*.pyc

# Misc editor/OS noise
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
